// conn_global_nil_init.cla: final-review wave regression pin for C1
// (clarusc/lower.cla's lowGlobalVarDecl). A global `connection` declared
// WITH a written `= nil` initializer used to lower that literal `nil`
// straight through (ExNilLit -> 0) instead of the slot+1 value every
// other global connection gets -- the connection-slot arm only ran in
// the "no initializer" `else if` branch, so a spelled-out `= nil` global
// stayed permanently nil (`rtConnOpen`/`rtConnClose`'s own h == 0 check
// panics "use of nil connection" on first use) even though the checker
// accepts the declaration, the variable still owns a slot, and `on
// c.<event>` handlers still bind to it. c.close() needs no prior open()
// (rtConnClose only nil-checks h; closing a never-opened slot is
// idempotent, spec Ch12) -- calling it here and reaching the alert
// PROVES c's own slot value is non-nil: on the unfixed compiler this
// program panics with exit 3 ("use of nil connection") before ever
// printing anything.
var c: connection = nil

on App.startCLI(args: list of string) {
    c.close()
    alert("conn global nil init ok")
    quit 0
}
